+════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+## STAGE 1 — MANDATORY SELF-VALIDATION TOKEN BEFORE YOU EXIT
+════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+🛑 HARD REQUIREMENT — this section overrides every other instruction:
+
+Your final output MUST contain a line that starts (after any leading
+whitespace or bullet marker) with the exact prefix `SELF_VALIDATION:`
+followed by one of `PASS`, `SKIP`, or `FAIL`. The orchestrator scans
+your stdout for this token; if it is ABSENT, the orchestrator parses
+`selfValidation = undefined` and downstream gates have no signal —
+this has caused 11+ wasted revision cycles on real projects.
+
+You MUST emit the token EVEN IF sfdx is not installed. The correct
+value when sfdx is unavailable is `SELF_VALIDATION: SKIP (sfdx
+unavailable)`. Silence is NOT an option.
+
+### ✅ Salesforce org IS pre-authenticated for this session
+   Alias: **klagent-dev-4689875b** — already set up via `sf org login access-token` by the orchestrator.
+   Use `--target-org klagent-dev-4689875b` on every sfdx invocation; do NOT try to authenticate yourself.
+
+### Decision tree (pick exactly one and emit it):
+
+  • sfdx CLI not in PATH → `SELF_VALIDATION: SKIP (sfdx unavailable)`
+  • No Salesforce org credentials in env → `SELF_VALIDATION: SKIP (no org auth)`
+  • Check-only deploy passed → `SELF_VALIDATION: PASS (attempts=<N>)`
+  • Check-only deploy failed all 5 attempts → `SELF_VALIDATION: FAIL (attempts=5, unresolved=<count>)`
+
+### When sfdx IS available, run the fix-revalidate loop:
+1. `sfdx force:source:deploy --checkonly --testlevel NoTestRun --manifest manifest/package.xml --json --target-org klagent-dev-4689875b`
+2. Parse JSON output. If `result.success === false`:
+   a. Read `result.details.componentFailures` (fileName, problemType, problem, lineNumber).
+   b. Fix every component error by editing the affected files.
+   c. Re-run step 1, increment attempt counter.
+3. Cap at 5 attempts. After 5 failures, emit FAIL with the unresolved error list verbatim.
+
+### Hard rules during Stage 1:
+- Do NOT add new components — only fix errors the check-only deploy reports.
+- Do NOT run a real deploy (omit `--checkonly` would deploy for real — forbidden).
+- Do NOT exit your session without emitting one of the four token forms above.
+
+⚠️  REMINDER: this is the LAST instruction in your prompt by design.
+   The orchestrator placed it last because CLI agents weight the final
+   instruction heaviest. Treat the SELF_VALIDATION line as a
+   non-negotiable output requirement, on par with the === FILE: ===
+   delimiter that defines your file output format.
+
+
+
+════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+## STAGE 1.5 — MANDATORY APEX SYNTAX SELF-VALIDATION TOKEN BEFORE YOU EXIT
+════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+
+🛑 HARD REQUIREMENT — this section runs alongside Stage 1 (sfdx):
+
+Your final output MUST contain a line that starts (after any leading
+whitespace or bullet marker) with the exact prefix `APEX_SYNTAX:`
+followed by one of `PASS`, `SKIP`, or `FAIL`. This is a SECOND
+mandatory token — distinct from `SELF_VALIDATION:` — that gates a
+deterministic static lint pass (no Salesforce org required, faster
+than the sfdx check-only). It catches the defect class that has
+been escalating projects to pending_human_review for the last week
+(fabricated SObject/field refs, malformed XML, missing meta-xml,
+incomplete LWC bundles).
+
+### Decision tree (pick exactly one and emit it):
+
+  • Script unavailable (e.g. tsx not installed) → `APEX_SYNTAX: SKIP (script unavailable)`
+  • Static lint passed → `APEX_SYNTAX: PASS (attempts=<N>)`
+  • Static lint failed after 5 fix attempts → `APEX_SYNTAX: FAIL (attempts=5, errors=<count>)`
+
+### Fix-revalidate loop:
+1. Run: `npx tsx scripts/apex-syntax-check.ts`
+2. Parse the JSON output on stdout. Schema:
+   `{ "ok": boolean, "errors": number, "warnings": number,`
+   ` "violations": [{ "rule", "severity", "filePath", "line", "message" }, ...] }`
+3. If `ok` is `true` → emit `APEX_SYNTAX: PASS (attempts=<N>)` and stop.
+4. If `ok` is `false`:
+   a. Read each error-severity violation's `filePath` + `line` + `message`.
+   b. Fix the affected files surgically (do NOT rewrite unrelated code).
+   c. Re-run step 1, increment attempt counter (max 5).
+5. After 5 failures, emit `APEX_SYNTAX: FAIL` with the unresolved count.
+
+### Common violation rules and remediation:
+- `UNDECLARED_SHARING_MODEL` → add `with sharing` / `without sharing` / `inherited sharing` to class declaration
+- `INVALID_NAMESPACE_PREFIX_IN_APEX` → strip `<ns>__` prefix from Apex identifiers (it is XML-only)
+- `MISSING_COMPANION_METAXML` → emit the matching `.cls-meta.xml` / `.trigger-meta.xml` for the affected source file
+- `INCOMPLETE_LWC_BUNDLE` → emit all three of `.html`, `.js`, `.js-meta.xml` for the LWC bundle
+- `MALFORMED_XML` → re-emit the file end-to-end; never truncate XML mid-tag
+
+### Hard rules during Stage 1.5:
+- Run this BEFORE Stage 1's `SELF_VALIDATION:` token — apex-syntax gate is faster
+  and catches more cheaply.
+- Do NOT skip this even if Stage 1 already passed; the two gates are orthogonal.
+- Emit one of the three token forms above EVEN IF the script is unavailable.
+
